Online data sources
-------------------

These are downloaded when asked for, and kept in the cache; none is
distributed with the program.

CelesTrak (https://celestrak.org): current orbital elements of
  satellites, by group and by catalogue number (File > Add Satellites),
  from the US Space Force's catalogue (space-track.org). CelesTrak's data
  may be used freely; it asks to be credited. Attribution: "Orbital
  elements: CelesTrak"

Downloadable data packs
-----------------------

The data packs offered in the program (File > Data Packs, hosted at
https://github.com/marutan/terrasoar-packs) are not part of the program;
each carries its licence notices in its licences/ folder. They contain:

bluemarble-full: the Blue Marble image above at full resolution
  (world.topo.bathy.200407.3x21600x10800.jpg). Public domain (NASA).

bluemarble-monthly: Blue Marble Next Generation with topography and
  bathymetry for each month of 2004, NASA Earth Observatory, at
  5400 x 2700 pixels
  (world.topo.bathy.200401.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200402.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200403.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200404.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200405.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200406.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200407.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200408.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200409.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200410.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200411.3x5400x2700.jpg
  world.topo.bathy.200412.3x5400x2700.jpg).
  Public domain (NASA). Attribution: "Blue Marble: NASA Earth
  Observatory"

shoreline-full: GSHHG 2.3.7 above with its high and full resolutions
  (gshhg-shp-2.3.7.zip). GNU LGPL v3 or later.

geoid-egm2008-fine: the EGM2008 geoid above at its 2.5' grid
  (us_nga_egm08_25.tif). Public domain (NGA).

geoid-osgm15 ("UK grids"): OSGM15, Ordnance Survey's geoid model for
  Ordnance Datum Newlyn, Great Britain (uk_os_OSGM15_GB.tif as
  distributed by PROJ, unchanged), and, from version 2015.2, OSTN15, the
  Ordnance Survey's transformation between OSGB36 and ETRS89 in its NTv2
  form (uk_os_OSTN15_NTv2_OSGBtoETRS.tif as distributed by PROJ,
  unchanged). BSD 2-Clause licence (Ordnance Survey, via PROJ).
  Attribution: "OSGM15: Ordnance Survey", "OSTN15: Ordnance Survey"

vmap0-boundaries, vmap0-hydrography-*, vmap0-transportation,
vmap0-population, vmap0-elevation-*, vmap0-vegetation-*, vmap0-other:
  Vector Map Level 0 (VMAP0), edition 5 (2000), National Imagery and
  Mapping Agency, now the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA),
  converted by tools/packager. Its four libraries, as kept by the
  University of Minnesota (https://geo.lib.umn.edu/gisdata/vmap0/):
  noamer.zip, eurnasia.zip, soamafr.zip, sasaus.zip. A US government
  work; releasability "UNRESTRICTED", access constraints none, use
  constraint "Cite National Imagery and Mapping Agency".
  Attribution: "Vector Map Level 0 (VMAP0), NGA"
  These packs leave out every feature that README1.TXT of the source
  names as ESRI's intellectual property.

vmap0-admin: the first-order administrative boundaries and named
  administrative areas of VMAP0 edition 5 (the same files). Copyright (C)
  1992-2000 ESRI and its licensors; ESRI Data License Agreement (internal
  or non-commercial use only; README1.TXT and FGDC_DAT.TXT, which must
  accompany it, are in its licences/ folder).
  Attribution: "Administrative areas: Vector Map Level 0 (VMAP0), NGA;
  (C) 1992-2000 ESRI and its licensors"

Every VMAP0 pack carries README1.TXT and FGDC_DAT.TXT of each library it
uses, unchanged, and tools/packager/notices/vmap0.txt.

wdbii: the World Data Bank II borders and rivers distributed with GSHHG
  2.3.7 above (gshhg-shp-2.3.7.zip, its WDBII_shp folder). GNU LGPL v3 or
  later. Attribution: "Borders and rivers: WDBII via GSHHG 2.3.7,
  P. Wessel and W. H. F. Smith (LGPL)"

naturalearth-10m: Natural Earth 1:10m vectors, version 5.1.2
  (ne_10m_rivers_lake_centerlines.geojson ne_10m_lakes.geojson
  ne_10m_populated_places.geojson ne_10m_roads.geojson
  ne_10m_railroads.geojson ne_10m_airports.geojson ne_10m_ports.geojson
  ne_10m_time_zones.geojson ne_10m_admin_1_states_provinces_lines.geojson
  ne_10m_geography_regions_elevation_points.geojson), simplified and
  tiled. Public domain. Attribution: "Made with Natural Earth"

naturalearth-relief, naturalearth-hypsometric, naturalearth-shaded-relief:
  Natural Earth's 1:10m raster maps, version 2.0.0, 21600 x 10800 pixels
  (NE1_HR_LC_SR_W_DR.zip, HYP_HR_SR_OB_DR.zip, SR_HR.zip), tiled. Public
  domain. Attribution: "Made with Natural Earth"

blackmarble: Black Marble, the Earth at night, NASA Earth Observatory from
  Suomi NPP VIIRS data, 2012 and 2016 at 3 km (BlackMarble_2012_3km_geo.tif,
  BlackMarble_2016_3km_geo.tif), tiled. Public domain (NASA). Attribution:
  "Black Marble: NASA Earth Observatory"

ourairports: OurAirports' airports, runways and navigation aids as of
  2026-11-22 (airports.csv, runways.csv, navaids.csv), dedicated to the
  public domain under the Unlicense. Attribution: "Airports: OurAirports"

names: populated places and major features from the US Board on
  Geographic Names' databases: for the United States, USGS GNIS Domestic
  Names of 2026-11-02 (DomesticNames_National_Text.zip); elsewhere, NGA's
  GEOnet Names Server feature class files of 2026-09-03
  (Populated_Places.zip, Hypsographic.zip, Hydrographic.zip, Undersea.zip),
  with NGA's disclaimer (in the pack's licences/ folder). US government
  works, public domain. Attribution: "Names: USGS GNIS, NGA GNS"

elevation-etopo-30s: ETOPO 2022 Global Relief Model, 30 arc-second surface
  elevation, version 1 (ETOPO_2022_v1_30s_N90W180_surface.tif), resampled
  to 30.1″ tiles; NOAA NCEI, CC0 1.0. Attribution: "Elevation: ETOPO 2022,
  NOAA NCEI"

gebco-w180-w90, gebco-w90-0, gebco-0-e90, gebco-e90-e180: the GEBCO_2026
  Grid, ice surface elevation (gebco_2026_geotiff.zip), a quarter of the
  world each, resampled to 15.1″ tiles; GEBCO Compilation Group, public
  domain, not for navigation (GEBCO_Grid_terms_of_use.pdf in each pack's
  licences/ folder). Attribution: "Bathymetry: GEBCO Compilation Group
  (2026) GEBCO 2026 Grid"

The raw files of every pack are kept, with their licences, in
https://github.com/marutan/terrasoar-packs-sources.

The source tree also has test data that is not distributed:
tests/data/geodtest-sample.dat, a sample of C. F. F. Karney's "Test set
for geodesics", CC0 1.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.32156; and, in
tests/support/nationalgriddata.h, the Ordnance Survey's OSTN15 test
points (TP01 to TP40 and their National Grid coordinates, from the
OSTN15 developer pack), BSD 2-Clause licence as OSTN15 itself; and
tests/data/kml/gdal/, KML test files from GDAL's autotest suite (MIT
licence), among them Google's "KML Samples" from the KML documentation
(Google, CC BY 4.0). tests/data/vmap0/ is one tile (L/H) of VMAP0
edition 5's SOAMAFR library, clipped by tools/fixtures/make_vmap0_fixture.py
with ESRI's features left out: a US government work (NGA), as above.

tests/orbits/data/: SGP4-VER.TLE and tcppver.out, the verification test
set and reference output of D. A. Vallado, P. Crawford, R. Hujsak and
T. S. Kelso, "Revisiting Spacetrack Report #3" (AIAA 2006-6753), as
redistributed by python-sgp4 2.27 (Copyright (c) 2012-2016 Brandon Rhodes,
MIT licence); and stations.tle, stations.json and gps-ops.tle, CelesTrak
element sets of 2026-11-20 (free to use, credit CelesTrak).

tests/data/kml/schema/, schemas for checking the KML Terra Soar writes:
ogckml22.xsd and atom-author-link.xsd, the OGC KML 2.2 schema (Copyright
(c) 2008 Open Geospatial Consortium; OGC Software Notice,
https://www.ogc.org/legal/), with its xAL import pointed at the local
copy; xAL.xsd, OASIS xAL 2.0 (Copyright (c) OASIS Open 2002; OASIS
copyright notice). terrasoar-gx.xsd and kml-and-gx.xsd are Terra Soar's
own.

